# Per-run wrk2 stdout is large (settle + overdrive + 5 cal probes + 5
# retries + validation + 5 measurement runs × 7 targets ≈ 100 files
# of ~5–10 KB each). Keep it on disk for forensic re-reads but don't
# carry it in git — every iteration would balloon the repo.
*/RAW/

# Server stdout/stderr lives next to RAW; same logic.
*/*.server.stdout
*/*.server.stderr

# What we DO commit per run, so each headline is interpretable
# without re-running:
#   summary.md          — the canonical headline table + run conditions
#   env.json            — host fingerprint + image digests
#   <target>-<cfg>.json — aggregated per-target stats (peak rps,
#                         medians + σ per percentile, run-by-run rps)
#   integrity.md        — response-byte integrity gate result
